---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: When the release pull request merges
    accDescr: Where the variable RELEASE_MERGE is daily, as in the blueprint, the release bot merges every release by itself. The run of a merge into main only keeps the release pull request current, unless the merge fixes a vulnerability, which merges at once. The daily run, which GitHub starts from 02:25 UTC on, at present usually hours later, merges it once its checks pass, unless a release went out that day already. A run of Release that you start by hand releases at once, for a fix that can't wait. With maintainer, the default of a new repository, you merge it, and only a release of dependency updates merges itself, once a day. The Rollout then brings the release to every repository that follows the blueprint.

    pr["`The release pull request collects<br>what merged since the last release`"]
    setting{"`RELEASE_MERGE`"}
    you["`You merge it; a release of dependency<br>updates merges itself once a day`"]
    event{"Which run of<br>the release bot?"}
    push["`A merge into *main*: it waits,<br>unless it fixes a vulnerability`"]
    daily["`The daily run, from 02:25 UTC on, unless<br>a release went out that day already`"]
    hand["`You start Release by hand,<br>for a fix that can't wait`"]
    merged["`It merges once its checks pass`"]
    rollout["`The Rollout brings it to every repository`"]

    pr --> setting
    setting -- "maintainer" --> you
    setting -- "daily" --> event
    event --> push
    event --> daily
    event --> hand
    daily --> merged
    hand --> merged
    you --> merged
    merged --> rollout

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class pr,push,daily bot
    class you,hand you
    class merged,rollout done
